(95, '2026-01-05 14:58:37', 'mjjq4uxzv7a7nkyd06l', 'message', '{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I can\\u2019t make the change for you, but I\\u2019ll guide you step by step.\\n\\nTo center your logo in the header (block theme):\\n\\n1. Go to **Appearance \\u2192 Editor** (Site Editor).\\n2. Click **Templates** or **Template Parts** \\u2192 open **Header**.\\n3. Click on the **Header** area to select it.\\n4. Select the **Row** or **Group** block that contains your logo and menu.\\n5. In the right settings panel:\\n   - Set **Justification \\/ Alignment** to **Center**.\\n6. If your menu is next to the logo:\\n   - Move the **Site Logo** block into its own **Row**.\\n   - Keep only the logo in that row.\\n   - Set that row\\u2019s alignment to **Center**.\\n7. Resize the logo if needed using the **Logo block settings**.\\n8. Click **Save**.\\n\\nIf your header has multiple sections (left menu, center logo, right icons), tell me and I\\u2019ll guide you for that layout specifically.\",\"followup\":\"\",\"pageSuggestion\":\"site-editor.php\",\"agent\":{\"id\":\"agent1\",\"name\":\"Support Specialist\",\"role\":\"WordPress Expert\",\"avatar\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"c2136734-a9ae-485e-a190-706e5615dce5\",\"firstSeen\":\"1\"}', 1),
