(100, '2026-01-05 14:58:37', 'mjjqhu3sgi8q1lpvav6', 'message', '{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I can\\u2019t change it for you yet, but I\\u2019ll guide you step by step.\\n\\nYou\\u2019re using a block theme, so this is controlled in the Header template.\\n\\nDo this:\\n\\n1. Go to **Appearance \\u2192 Editor** (Site Editor)\\n2. Open **Templates \\u2192 Header** (or Template Parts \\u2192 Header)\\n3. Click the **Header** area until you see the main container (usually a **Group** or **Row** block)\\n4. If the logo is on a second row:\\n   - Select the outer **Group**\\n   - Change its layout to **Row** (right sidebar \\u2192 Layout)\\n5. Inside the same Row, place these blocks:\\n   - **Site Logo**\\n   - **Site Title**\\n   - **Navigation**\\n6. Make sure they are all inside the **same Row block** (not separate rows)\\n7. Use **Justification: Space between** or **Align items: Center** if needed\\n8. Save\\n\\nIf the logo is inside a different block:\\n- Drag the **Site Logo** block into the same Row as the menu and title.\\n\\nIf you want, tell me:\\n- Are you using **one Row or multiple Rows** in the header?\\nI\\u2019ll give more precise steps.\",\"followup\":\"\",\"pageSuggestion\":\"site-editor.php\",\"agent\":{\"id\":\"agent1\",\"name\":\"Support Specialist\",\"role\":\"WordPress Expert\",\"avatar\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"0d0abc4d-1a2c-45a0-972d-376874c8b4f3\"}', 1),
