(105, '2026-01-05 14:58:37', 'mjjqy0mk9c7sfpl9amj', 'message', '{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I can\\u2019t adjust it for you yet, but I\\u2019ll guide you.\\n\\nTo center the logo exactly in the header (block theme):\\n\\n- Go to **Appearance \\u2192 Editor \\u2192 Header**\\n- Click the **Header** area, then select the **block that contains the logo** (often a Row or Group)\\n- In the **block settings (right panel)**:\\n  - Set **Justification \\/ Alignment** to **Center**\\n\\nIf you have **three items** (menu \\u2013 logo \\u2013 buttons):\\n\\n- Select the **Row** block that holds all three\\n- Set **Justify content** to **Space between**\\n- Click the **logo block**\\n- Set its **Alignment** to **Center**\\n\\nIf it\\u2019s still off-center:\\n- Make sure the left and right items have **similar width**\\n- Avoid extra padding or margins on the logo block\\n\\nTell me what blocks you\\u2019re using (Row, Columns, Group), and I\\u2019ll give exact settings.\",\"followup\":\"\",\"pageSuggestion\":\"\",\"agent\":{\"id\":\"agent1\",\"name\":\"Support Specialist\",\"role\":\"WordPress Expert\",\"avatar\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"f9d44fcf-aa49-4118-9a41-c5e8f665bc2e\"}', 1),
