(125, '2026-01-05 14:58:37', 'mjjranvq1xgiui1t8pki', 'message', '{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I can\\u2019t fix it for you directly yet, but I\\u2019ll guide you.\\n\\nSince you\\u2019re using a block theme, the logo is usually off\\u2011center because of the header layout.\\n\\nTry this:\\n\\n**Option 1: Use a centered header layout**\\n- Go to **Appearance \\u2192 Editor**\\n- Open **Templates \\u2192 Header**\\n- Click the main header block (often a **Group** or **Row**)\\n- In the right sidebar, set **Justification \\/ Alignment** to **Center**\\n- Make sure the **Site Logo** block itself is set to **Align: Center**\\n\\n**Option 2: Fix left\\/right spacing (most common issue)**\\n- Select the **Row** that contains the logo and menu\\n- Check if there are **3 columns** (Menu \\u2013 Logo \\u2013 Icons)\\n- Make sure the left and right columns have **equal width**\\n- Remove extra padding or margin from left or right blocks\\n\\n**Option 3: Absolute center (logo only)**\\n- Select the **Site Logo**\\n- Turn off **Wide \\/ Full width** if enabled\\n- Set margins to **0** on all sides\\n\\nIf it\\u2019s still not centered, tell me:\\n- Is the menu on one side or both sides of the logo?\\n- Are there icons (search, social, buttons) in the header?\\n\\nI\\u2019ll give you the exact fix.\",\"followup\":\"\",\"pageSuggestion\":\"site-editor.php\",\"agent\":{\"id\":\"agent1\",\"name\":\"Support Specialist\",\"role\":\"WordPress Expert\",\"avatar\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"53d1c830-8d0f-4702-b43e-bde29fc00155\"}', 1),
