(130, '2026-01-05 14:58:37', 'mjjrcuztwj8t9ibbpe', 'message', '{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"To check that the left and right columns have equal width (Block Theme):\\n\\n**In the Site Editor:**\\n- Go to **Appearance \\u2192 Editor**.\\n- Click the section with the two columns.\\n- Select the **Columns** block (click the parent container).\\n- In the right sidebar **Settings**:\\n  - Make sure **Layout** is set to **Equal width** (or remove any custom % widths).\\n\\n**Check each column:**\\n- Click the left column \\u2192 Settings \\u2192 confirm **Width** is not set to a custom value.\\n- Click the right column \\u2192 do the same.\\n\\n**Quick visual check:**\\n- Enable **List View** and confirm both columns are under the same Columns block with no custom widths.\\n\\nIf you want, tell me where this section is (header, page, template) and I\\u2019ll guide you exactly.\",\"followup\":\"\",\"pageSuggestion\":\"\",\"agent\":{\"id\":\"agent1\",\"name\":\"Support Specialist\",\"role\":\"WordPress Expert\",\"avatar\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"9922f528-2889-49ba-b03f-e12281cf1d46\"}', 1),
